    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Semiconductor innovation drives improvements to technologies that are critical to modern society.\r\nThe country that successfully accelerates semiconductor innovation is positioned to lead future\r\nsemiconductor-driven industries and benefit from the resulting economic growth. It is our view\r\nthat a next generation infrastructure is necessary to accelerate and enhance semiconductor innovation\r\nin the U.S. In this paper, we propose such an advanced infrastructure composed of a national\r\nnetwork of facilities with enhancements in technology and business models. These enhancements\r\nenable application-driven and challenge-based research and development, and ensure that facilities\r\nare accessible and sustainable. The main tenets are: a challenge-driven operational model, a\r\nnext-generation infrastructure to serve that operational model, technology innovations needed for\r\nadvanced facilities to speed up learning cycles, and innovative cost-effective business models for\r\nsustainability. Ultimately, the expected outcomes of such a participatory, scalable, and sustainable\r\nnation-level advanced infrastructure will have tremendous impact on government, industry, and\r\nacademia alike.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Gottscho, R., Levine, E., Liu, T.-J. K., McIntyre, P., Mitra, S., Murmann, B., Rabaey, J., Salahuddin, S., Shih, W., and Wong, H.-S. P. (2022). Innovating at Speed and at Scale: A Next Generation Infrastructure for Accelerating Semiconductor Technologies. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/xt622tg6135",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
